    "bubble_choice_description": "Add a count message, a filter summary label, and a friendly empty state to a showtimes list.",
    "long_instructions": "## Movie Showtime\r\n\r\n**Goal:**\r\nEnhance the movie showtimes view with clear **transparency cues** so users always know what they're seeing, what filters are active, and what happens when nothing matches.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n1. **Open `script.js`.**\r\n   Find the `render()` function. This is where the movie list is built.\r\n\r\n2. **Add three messages to improve clarity:**\r\n\r\n   * **Count message:**\r\n     Update `#countMessage` to show how many results are displayed out of the total.\r\n     Example: `Showing 3 of 6 results`\r\n   * **Filter label:**\r\n     Update `#filterLabel` to summarize the rule being used.\r\n     Example: `Filter: showtimes after 6 PM`\r\n   * **Empty-state message:**\r\n     If no results match, show a friendly message in `#emptyMessage`, such as:\r\n\r\n     > “No showtimes found for this selection.”\r\n     > Otherwise, hide it.\r\n\r\n3. **Test your work.**\r\n\r\n4. **Use AI to check your reasoning:**\r\n\r\n   * \"Explain what my loop is doing each time it runs.\"\r\n   * \"Check if my count message still works when there are no results.\"\r\n   * \"Suggest a friendlier way to say 'No results found.'\"\r\n\r\n",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Movie Showtimes — Adding Transparency</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\" />\n</head>\n<body>\n\n  <h2>Movie Showtimes</h2>\n\n  <p id=\"countMessage\"></p>\n  <p id=\"filterLabel\"></p>\n\n  <ul id=\"movieList\"></ul>\n  <p id=\"emptyMessage\"></p>\n\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "body {\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n  background-color: #f9f9f9;\n  color: #222;\n  margin: 40px;\n}\n\nh2 {\n  color: #333;\n}\n\n#movieList {\n  list-style: none;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\n#movieList li {\n  background: #fff;\n  margin: 8px 0;\n  padding: 8px 12px;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n}\n\np {\n  margin: 6px 0;\n}\n\n#emptyMessage {\n  color: #666;\n  font-style: italic;\n}\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "// --- Sample data (toggle to test) ---\nconst movies = [\n  { title: \"Moon Harbor\", time: \"6:15 PM\" },\n  { title: \"Granite Peak\", time: \"7:00 PM\" },\n  { title: \"Neon River\", time: \"9:10 PM\" }\n];\n\nfunction render() {\n  const list = document.getElementById(\"movieList\");\n  list.innerHTML = \"\";\n\n  // show only movies after 6 PM\n  const results = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < movies.length; i++) {\n    \n    const movie = movies[i];\n    if (movie.time >= \"6:00 PM\") {\n      results.push(movie);\n      const li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n      li.textContent = movie.title + \" — \" + movie.time;\n      list.appendChild(li);\n    }\n  }\n\n\n  \n}\n\nrender();\n\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "1",
        "2",
        "3"
      ]
    },
